<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  forest_pillars_robot_duo.sdf - forest_pillars_robot.sdf with the two-pad robot
  (robot_dock_duo) for the multi-drone patrol (tools/multi_drone). Made from it by
  swapping the robot model and world name only; regenerate the same way if
  forest_pillars_robot.sdf changes. Its header follows.

  forest_pillars_robot.sdf - GENERATED by gen_forest.py, do not edit by hand.
  Generated with: seed=1 trees=30 size=15 min-gap=2
  (pass the same values as gen_forest.py options to regenerate; XML comments can't contain two dashes)

  30 cylinder trunks in a 15 x 15 m square centred on the spawn point,
  >= 2 m apart (surface to surface), 2 m clear around spawn,
  corners of a 10 m patrol square kept clear. Trunks are 6-10 m tall.
  Landing pad: on the robot_dock model (B2 class, pad 0.665 m up) at E=0 N=0; spawn drone 0 at "0,0.5,0.67" and drone 1 at "0,-0.5,0.67" (pads 0 and 1).

  Link into PX4 once:
    ln -s ~/dev/DroneSwarm-MAP-SAR/src/las_offboard/worlds/forest_pillars_robot_duo.sdf \
          ~/dev/PX4-Autopilot/Tools/simulation/gz/worlds/forest_pillars_robot_duo.sdf
  Coordinates: ENU, x = East, y = North, metres; spawn at (0, 0).
-->
